  "suite_sha256": "420cc0126b6f444687199662edc998461bb33cad1c917ac78fe7e00eb587681a",
  "rationale": "The previous counterexamples revealed critical failures in tenant isolation (stock leaking across tenants), idempotency (retries consuming stock, double releases restoring stock), payload binding (conflicts ignored), and validation (negative/float/over-max accepted). The new suite targets these specific failure modes: 1) Verifies that Tenant A's stock is unaffected by Tenant B's reservations (fixing the 'available: 8' bug). 2) Confirms that duplicate keys with identical payloads do not consume additional inventory. 3) Ensures double releases are idempotent and do not inflate stock beyond 10. 4) Validates strict conflict detection for changed quantities. 5) Re-enforces boundary conditions for invalid inputs. These cases directly address the observed defects without duplicating existing test structures.",
  "origin": "live Fetch.ai / ASI:One; fresh context, implementation withheld"
